- 1 lb (weight) = 1 lb × (1 slug / 32 ft/s²)

So, mass flow rate in slugs per yard:

= 37.5 lb/yd × (1 slug / 32 lb) = 37.5 / 32 = 1.1719 slugs/yd

Now convert yd to ft: 1 yd = 3 ft → per foot: divide by 3

So, mass flow rate in slugs per foot = 1.1719 / 3 ≈ 0.3906 slugs/ft

Now velocity = 88 ft/sec

So force = mass flow rate × velocity  
= 0.3906 slugs/ft × 88 ft/sec  
= 34.37 lb-force (lbf)

So the **force required is approximately 34.4 lbf**

